# UI Spec (`packages/ui`)

**Do not use Figma** for UI design or frontend implementation in this repo. The canonical UI component library is `packages/ui`.

## Mandatory: reference component examples

Before designing or implementing **any** portal page, screen, or shared UI component:

1. Open `packages/ui/src/components/ui/` — find the **relevant shadcn/ui primitive** (accordion, alert, alert-dialog, avatar, badge, breadcrumb, button, calendar, card, chart, checkbox, collapsible, combobox, command, context-menu, dialog, dropdown-menu, hover-card, input, input-group, input-otp, label, menubar, pagination, popover, progress, radio-group, resizable, scroll-area, select, separator, sheet, sidebar, skeleton, slider, sonner, switch, table, tabs, textarea, toggle, toggle-group, tooltip)
2. Reference the component props and variants from the source files in `packages/ui/src/components/ui/<name>.tsx`
3. Implement in `packages/ui` or portal apps by **following** shadcn/ui patterns; do not invent one-off patterns.

## When to read

Before designing screens (`ui-designer`) or implementing UI (`nextjs-frontend`), read:

1. `packages/ui/src/index.ts` — **exported components (primary reference)**
2. `packages/ui/src/components/ui/*.tsx` — shadcn/ui primitives and their APIs
3. `packages/ui/styles/globals.css` — design tokens (colors, radius)
4. `packages/ui/` — shadcn style, icon library configuration

## Rules

- **Components:** Only use primitives defined in `packages/ui/src/components/ui/`. Map to `packages/ui` or app `components/ui/` — keep APIs aligned with shadcn/ui standards.
- **Composition:** Follow shadcn/ui patterns for ERP pages (spacing, variants, nested layout). ERP pages are not marketing landings — prefer data-dense patterns.
- **Tokens:** Match CSS variables from `packages/ui/styles/globals.css`. Do not invent one-off hex colors.
- **Variants:** Follow shadcn/ui usage patterns (Button, Badge, Table, Dialog, Sheet, etc.).
- **Icons:** `lucide-react` per packages/ui `components.json` (portals may use `@tabler/icons-react` in shells only if already established in `packages/ui`).
- **New patterns:** If a screen needs a primitive or composition not in `packages/ui`, **add the component to packages/ui first**, then propagate to portal apps.
- **No Figma MCP:** Do not call Figma tools, sync to Figma, or block on Figma node IDs.

## Portal implementation

| Layer | Location |
|-------|----------|
| Shared UI components | `packages/ui/` |
| App routes & feature UI | `apps/admin/`, `apps/merchant/`, `apps/store/` |
| Screen wireframes | `docs/design/<feature>.md` |

Design docs describe layout and behavior; **visual and compositional constraints come from shadcn/ui patterns in packages/ui**.
